`python3 run_check.py` now passes with all expected values:

```
seeded 10 orders into data/service.db (env=dev)
OK - all checks passed
```

What was wrong (all in the service code; `run_check.py` and `seed.py` untouched):

1. **`svc/config.py`** — `SVC_ENV` defaulted to `prod`, so `config.load()` pointed at `/var/lib/svc/service.db`, which isn't writable on a dev machine. That was the original `PermissionError`. The default is now `dev` (matching the docstrings: dev = local sqlite under `./data`). The public API shape is unchanged.

2. **`svc/db.py`** — the `orders` table never declared the `currency` column that `seed.py` inserts and both reports filter on, so seeding would have failed next.

3. **`svc/reports.py`, `revenue_between`** — it compared `created_at < end`, which excludes the entire final day. March 31 orders (gamma 90,000 + beta 45,000) were dropped, yielding 185,000 instead of the agreed 320,000. It now uses `created_at < date(?, '+1 day')` so both endpoints are inclusive.

4. **`svc/reports.py`, `top_customers`** — offset was `page * page_size` instead of `(page - 1) * page_size`, so page 1 started at row 3. Pages now return the expected `[acme 90k, gamma 90k, beta 75k]` and `[theta 65k, delta 10k, zeta 5k]` (with the acme-before-gamma tie-break on name).

I also verified the boundary behavior doesn't leak across months: April only counts delta's 10,000, and the EUR order is only counted when `currency="EUR"`.
